{"title":"1997 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/6/526715fb9a391a9557276efc30584ee731b08f18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1,p_2,p_3,...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"11\" /> be the prime numbers listed in increasing order, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f1249ad95b7682b8316ad21de8ce4ee9fdcf93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> be a real number between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. For positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, define\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8cf2d0e027bf6ce4aa7ac1ee52966e38b73d548.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{k}=\\begin{cases}0&amp;\\text{ if }x_{k-1}=0\\\\ \\left\\{\\frac{p_{k}}{x_{k-1}}\\right\\}&amp;\\text{ if }x_{k-1}\\ne0\\end{cases}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"220\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3df2919191b1220773d9b0142dec5c3528fd4c42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the fractional part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. (The fractional part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is given by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e0750000dbb8c44345a25e37db9debfc0c4d6f9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-\\lfloor{x}\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"19\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/1/d618c9b39b6f26bd5761aace8dfa1257de0a286e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor{x}\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> is the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.) Find, with proof, all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f1249ad95b7682b8316ad21de8ce4ee9fdcf93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/f/2cf5803872dbc90c625ca74f67515a77ec140b00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x_0&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" /> for which the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/7/b57eab14db6408db514dbf3970d4eefe54658c9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0,x_1,x_2,...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"11\" /> eventually becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle, and draw isosceles triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/9/fe95a8aa36ccc72c674ef67c7695846887a36d41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD, CAE, ABF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"145\" height=\"16\" /> externally to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/e/d8efab0f68cfe83cd75f01f951920f544da89d49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC, CA, AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" /> as their respective bases. Prove that the lines through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a9874ea56cf8fec1bd246793224fbcfaad17ab3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> perpendicular to the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70ba6a2b206c376acbdd994a290dd6c5d529ed89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{EF},\\overleftrightarrow{FD},\\overleftrightarrow{DE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"104\" height=\"25\" />, respectively, are concurrent.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Prove that for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, there exists a unique polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> with coefficients in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/8/028d44ae148dd9b11623822eccb55d187ce2ee0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{0,1,...,9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472d9a265a0dca53dd2023594dd8a3b738ee00ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(-2)=Q(-5)=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>To <i>clip</i> a convex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-gon means to choose a pair of consecutive sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/a/5aaa2452d9ce4302e49ed83896ce666bd63e981c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB, BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" /> and to replace them by three segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d27ebc6c6f351c7a804df80c8c36f210283108c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM, MN,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a520b80dced875a569a33003df12d5c1141c903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. In other words, one cuts off the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eec040384e5c85f020f622f50d8e77964e92879a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MBN$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> to obtain a convex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99cb3f3a8b3bbfc702c5863d16602a06cded535d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />-gon. A regular hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/f/d1f87397a1a9e553a7da9d6b590d1da2da5bb874.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> of area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is clipped to obtain a heptagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/4/bd404c07b0b0414e3b2cf6b80554ff87b9c3f4c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/4/bd404c07b0b0414e3b2cf6b80554ff87b9c3f4c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is clipped (in one of the seven possible ways) to obtain an octagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2eff3134cfcd590c32ac86c6371b5349d96fa716.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" />, and so on. Prove that no matter how the clippings are done, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c51a4acedda645113145d008dbfb50d35f1da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad61c1573fdae14b60adfc9737b6ba91b5e41a6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Prove that, for all positive real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/0/2d02bb2275100261109b043261e702124460a83e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/1/d8167712da65da7e7f96622dc154a2f9b1542ee1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a^3+b^3+abc}+\\frac{1}{b^3+c^3+abc}+\\frac{1}{a^3+c^3+abc} \\le \\frac{1}{abc}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"412\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Suppose the sequence of nonnegative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/a/48a4904106208329f63890b1ddf94653d0855c9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,...,a_{1997}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"109\" height=\"11\" /> satisfies \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/3/6e3b688d2099e8261dc37a092655f7f34e612154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i+a_j \\le a_{i+j} \\le a_i+a_j+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"218\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9a63aa9860b207551383e2545ceea778192756b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i, j \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5fcff7adcef84f70d5545e318d0dab0d82da867.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i+j \\le 1997$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" />. Show that there exists a real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c892c8177240782793e48eb977bd244642c695.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=\\lfloor{nx}\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" /> (the greatest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20fefac100f3453d26fcdc118b77bf8dda6b092b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />) for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/154b4cb8b79f1fb8de5395a1bf3564f8a98acc09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le n \\le 1997$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO\" title=\"1997 USAMO\">1997 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1997\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO\" title=\"1996 USAMO\">1996 USAMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO\" title=\"1998 USAMO\">1998 USAMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1997 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div